WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:08.267
Bottom line: standardize skills and MCP, then govern compatibility and ownership for each host.

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:12.533
Cowork uses a Microsoft 365 app package.

00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:16.867
Declarative agents use MCP or REST API actions.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:23.900
GitHub Copilot uses plugin packages with portable and client-specific parts.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:28.900
Reuse skill logic and MCP configuration where tested.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:36.800
Keep authentication, manifests, discovery and client-only components inside each host package.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:42.100
REST API actions remain supported in declarative agents.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:49.600
Agent Plugins 1.0 adds portability, while legacy GitHub Copilot plugins continue to load.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:53.700
Assign one owner per capability and service.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:02.967
Publish a host compatibility matrix, version each package, and add routes only when demand justifies lifecycle cost.
